ue. This is a finite numerical verification, not a proof of the Riemann Hypothesis. Still unchecked: the exact zero count up to height 1000, and the first-1000-zeros statement (which needs height about 1419).\n\nANSWER: All non-trivial zeros of \u03b6(s) with 0 < Im(s) \u2264 1000 lie on Re(s) = 1/2 (host check rh_zeros_on_line(1000, 1/2) == True); this is a finite check, not a proof of RH.", "op": "CONTRIBUTION", "prev": "b22f82597f19d72d4c718ac3055e709973a086c5aa6c4b4569596e8872ed68c3", "reason": "CRITICISM_FOUND", "receipt": "receipt_2a73b3da4f94447a801311d13fddc409", "row": "CT-a5cc7006c8fb06cec425", "row_seq": 5, "seq": 13, "target_row": "CT-e7a5d3e0ec52990f6e1f", "target_seq": 2}
